the simulation waveform is taken from vivado and the source code was written in systemverilog.

First, a reset is applied for two clock cycles to initialize the design and ensure the pipeline starts in an empty state.
After reset is released, a normal data transfer is performed by driving in_valid and out_ready high simultaneously.
This verifies that the pipeline can correctly accept and forward data when both sides are ready.

Next, a backpressure condition is created by keeping out_ready low while valid input data is presented.
This checks whether the pipeline correctly stores the incoming data and prevents additional transfers while the
downstream stage is stalled.

Finally, the recovery scenario is tested by asserting out_ready again. This allows the stored data to be released and
verifies that the pipeline resumes normal operation without losing or duplicating data.
A clock with a 10 ns period is generated throughout the simulation
